{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, sorry the file shares are slow. To narrow this down, could you tell us a few things: 1) Are you working in the office or from home over VPN today? Shared drives are normally slower over VPN, so large files are often better opened from OneDrive or SharePoint. 2) Is only the file shares slowness happening, or is everything slow, including websites and Teams? 3) Is it one particular shared drive or all of them? While you reply, please try these: disconnect and reconnect the VPN if you are on it, pause any large OneDrive sync or backup, and restart your computer if it has been on for several days. If it is still slow after that, let us know and we will look into it further.",
  "internal_note": "Sender: James O'Connor (user 8), Operations, Warehouse Supervisor, Chicago, usual hours 06:00-14:00 CT. Account active, no failed logins, not blocked, VPN enabled, mailbox 29.7% used. Only device BL-DT-0108 shows offline, last check-in 2026-10-11 01:04 UTC (about 20:04 CT on 10-10, outside usual hours), disk 78% free, no warnings, so disk is not the cause. Sign-ins for the last 14 days are all successful with Duo push, no anomalies; they alternate between corporate network (m365) and residential VPN. No evidence of compromise. Not yet known: whether today's session is VPN or office, whether all apps or only shares are slow, and which share. Per KB-015 the next step depends on those answers: if the whole office is slow or one share is slow for everyone, escalate to Tier 2. Otherwise apply the KB-015 fix steps. Reply from user needed before further action. Note the device appears offline in the device check, so confirm it is powered on and connected.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-015",
    "KB-017"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
